      "briefing": "## Your job\n\n- Packets dive toward your network. Check each one against the list.\n- **Denied?** Shoot it.\n- **Permitted?** Let it through.\n- Right call: +1 health (max 3). Wrong call: -1 health. At 0, the wave ends.\n\n## Read one entry\n\n> permit udp any host 192.168.5.9 eq 5060\n\n- **permit**: what to do with matches\n- **udp**: the protocol\n- **any**: the source\n- **host 192.168.5.9**: the destination\n- **eq 5060**: the port\n\n## Addresses\n\n- **any**: every address\n- **host 10.0.0.5**: exactly that one\n- **10.0.0.0/24**: 10.0.0.0 to 10.0.0.255\n\nAn entry matches only if **every** part matches.\n\n## Controls\n\n- Arrow keys move. Space fires.\n- The game never stops for a mistake. Each one is explained after the wave.\n- Simplified: IPv4 only, one packet at a time, no wildcard masks."
